---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="FAQs - GDGoC">
  <main>
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-center mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h1>
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is an algorithm?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">An algorithm is a step-by-step set of instructions or rules designed to solve a specific problem or perform a task.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is a programming language?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">A programming language is a formal language used to communicate instructions to a computer and create software programs. Examples include Python, JavaScript, and Java.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is the difference between frontend and backend development?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Frontend development focuses on the user interface and experience (what users see), while backend development deals with server-side logic, databases, and application functionality (behind the scenes).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is an IDE?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">An IDE (Integrated Development Environment) is a software application that provides tools for writing, testing, and debugging code, such as Visual Studio Code or PyCharm.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is version control?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Version control is a system that records changes to files over time, allowing you to track history and collaborate with others. Git is a popular version control system.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is open source software?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Open source software is software whose source code is freely available for anyone to view, use, modify, and distribute.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is a database?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">A database is an organized collection of data that can be easily accessed, managed, and updated. Examples include MySQL, MongoDB, and PostgreSQL.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is an API?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">An API (Application Programming Interface) is a set of rules that allows different software applications to communicate with each other.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is machine learning?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Machine learning is a field of artificial intelligence where computers learn from data and improve their performance over time without being explicitly programmed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow p-6">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">What is cloud computing?</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Cloud computing is the delivery of computing services (like storage, databases, and servers) over the internet, allowing users to access resources on demand.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>